IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §6.1, R-T3 (built 2026-09-15): the BLAME LIST.
--
-- A breach names every obligation that failed, not one of them — one entry
-- per failure, each with what was failed (the action and deadline missed, or
-- the reason declared), duplicates kept: the same party twice is two entries,
-- and the two ways are visible (RULED 2026-09-15: no dedup). Three places
-- produce a compound breach, and the traces below pin each:
--
--   * a BARRIER (`ONCE ALL HAVE`) with no LEST: every member that did not
--     complete is named, in ROLL order, each with its own deadline, and the
--     breach is anchored at the EARLIEST failure;
--   * a barrier WITH a LEST: the LEST runs once, anchored at the earliest
--     failure — not at the first failure in roll order — which shows up as
--     the reparation's deadline;
--   * `RAND`: when both sides are lost, both sides' failures are named, left
--     operand first.
--
-- And `BREACH BY` takes a LIST of parties as well as a party. A single
-- obligation's breach prints exactly as it always did.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign   HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Refund HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol
`tenants, reversed` MEANS LIST carol, bob, alice

-- 1. Two members fail: both are named, in roll order. Alice signs; Bob and
--    Carol never do. The breach is one record, anchored at the earliest miss
--    (both are 14 here), and it lists everyone who missed, each with the
--    action and deadline they missed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`all sign` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED

#TRACE `all sign` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 2. The same failure over the reversed roll: the same two parties, in the
--    reversed order. The order is the roll's, nothing else.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`all sign, reversed` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN `tenants, reversed`
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED

#TRACE `all sign, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 3. A later-in-roll member fails EARLIER in time. Carol, last on the roll,
--    has five days; Bob, before her, has fourteen. Neither signs. The
--    barrier's LEST is anchored at Carol's failure — revealed at day 8 — so
--    the landlord's three days to refund run out at day 11, and a refund at
--    day 12 is late. Anchored at the first failure in roll order (Bob's,
--    revealed at day 20) the refund would have been on time.
GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days allowed to` t MEANS IF t EQUALS carol THEN 5 ELSE 14

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered signing` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 3)

#TRACE `staggered signing` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 12
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- The same staggered deadlines with no LEST: the breach is anchored at the
-- earliest failure (Carol's deadline, day 5, revealed at day 8) and names
-- both non-completers in roll order — Bob before Carol, although Carol failed
-- first — each with their own deadline: Bob's 14, Carol's 5.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered signing, no reparation` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED

#TRACE `staggered signing, no reparation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 4. RAND of two single-party obligations, both missed: both failures are
--    named, left operand first. The anchor is the earliest breach as before
--    (here a tie, revealed by the same event, so the left one).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both sign` MEANS
    (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 14)
    RAND
    (PARTY bob   MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob)   WITHIN 14)

#TRACE `both sign` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- The same party on both sides of a RAND is named TWICE, once per way: Alice
-- missed the signing and Alice missed the refund, and the answer says both.
-- (Meng, 2026-09-15: "maybe we need to be able to say, 'well, Alice screwed
-- the pooch two different ways'".)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`alice twice` MEANS
    (PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 14)
    RAND
    (PARTY alice MUST Refund (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 14)

#TRACE `alice twice` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 5. BREACH BY a LIST of parties: the drafter names several, and the answer
--    names them as written — one entry each, in order, duplicates kept, each
--    carrying the BECAUSE.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`joint and several` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord
        MUST   Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord)
        WITHIN 3
        LEST   BREACH BY LIST alice, bob, alice BECAUSE "the tenants carry it"

#TRACE `joint and several` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- A computed LIST with nobody in it is refused at run time, by name: a breach
-- blames at least one party. (A literal empty list — `BY EMPTY` — is refused
-- when the file is checked; see not-ok/tc/breach-by-empty.l4.)
GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
nobody t MEANS FALSE

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`blame nobody` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord
        MUST   Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord)
        WITHIN 3
        LEST   BREACH BY filter nobody tenants

#TRACE `blame nobody` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 6. One member fails: the text is unchanged from before the blame set —
--    "party", singular, and one name.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`one misses` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED

#TRACE `one misses` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- 7. A party that is itself a LIST. `BY` then names the one party, not its
--    elements: the checker reads a LIST at the party type as that party
--    (and a LIST of such lists as several).
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC (LIST OF STRING) Step
`the pair delivers` MEANS
    PARTY (LIST "a", "b")
        MUST   deliver
        WITHIN 5
        LEST   BREACH BY (LIST "a", "b") BECAUSE "the pair did not deliver"

#TRACE `the pair delivers` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
